# Writing style

- Never use em dashes (`—`) in user-facing copy, metadata titles, dates, or comments that ship as content.
- Prefer natural punctuation: commas, periods, colons, parentheses, or a short rewrite.
- For date ranges, use `to` (e.g. `2025 to Present`, `2022 to 2024`), not em dashes.
- For page title templates, use a middle dot or pipe (e.g. `%s · Name`), not an em dash.

## Examples

```text
Bad:  I care about systems under load — clear interfaces matter.
Good: I care about systems under load: clear interfaces matter.
Good: I care about systems under load. Clear interfaces matter.

Bad:  2025 — Present
Good: 2025 to Present

Bad:  About — C V Tarun
Good: About · C V Tarun
```
